{# ——— The one date field in the product ———
   Included by every form that asks for a date: a service form row
   (`components/form-row.twig`), the account profile and the admin user
   editor. It is its own file rather than a branch inside form-row.twig
   because the profile and admin forms are hand-written layouts — leaving
   the markup in form-row.twig would have meant copying it, and a copied
   date input is how two "identical" date fields quietly diverge.

   The contract it renders:

     what a person sees and types → 06-10-2026   (DD-MM-YYYY)
     what the row stores          → 2026-10-06   (Y-m-d)

   `App\Service\ServiceDate` is the only thing allowed to convert between
   them, so `value` must already be in display form (the action hands it
   over via ServiceDate::display()). A plain `<input type="date">` is
   deliberately not used: it renders in whatever order the OS thinks is
   natural, so the same page would ask one user for 06-10-2026 and the next
   for 10-06-2026 — and six of October and ten of June are both legal
   answers to it. `type="text"` + `inputmode="numeric"` gives a phone a
   number pad, and `resources/js/date-field.js` supplies the dashes, the
   OS calendar and the client-side check against the very same message
   the server sends.

   With JavaScript off this is still a labelled, pattern-checked text field
   the server accepts — the calendar is an enhancement, not the mechanism.

   @var name string      form field name
   @var id string        input id (the label's `for`)
   @var label string     visible label text
   @var value string     current value, display form
   @var required bool
   @var error string     validation message, shown instead of the format hint #}
<div>
    <label for="{{ id }}" class="form-label">
        {{ label }}
        {% if required|default(false) %}<span class="text-danger-600">*</span>{% endif %}
    </label>

    <div class="date-field" data-date-field>
        <input id="{{ id }}" type="text" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ value|default('') }}"
               class="form-input date-field-input" data-date-input
               inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false"
               placeholder="06-10-2026" maxlength="10" pattern="[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{4}"
               aria-describedby="{{ id }}-hint"
               {% if required|default(false) %}required{% endif %}>
    </div>

    {# The hint is the format itself, read from ServiceDate rather than typed
       into each template — a form that hard-coded the words could drift away
       from the parser and quietly start asking for something it will then
       reject. #}
    {% if error|default('') %}
        <p class="form-error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
    {% else %}
        <p class="form-help" id="{{ id }}-hint">ফরম্যাট: {{ date_format() }} — যেমন 06-10-2026</p>
    {% endif %}
</div>